## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to enable rapid domain adaptation with privacy guarantees in a real-time environment, emphasizing latency constraints, privacy preservation, and robust rollback mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- Parameter-efficient adapters (LoRA/Adapters) for domain adaptation
- On-device fine-tuning with privacy guarantees (DP or federated learning)
- Streaming drift detection and safe rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: load base model, attach adapter for domain, fine-tune on small labeled set
function adaptDomain(model, domain, labeledData) {
  const adapter = new LoRAAdapter(model, { rank: 4, alpha: 8 });
  adapter.fineTune(labeledData, { privacy: 'DP-SGD', epochs: 3 });
  return adapter;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a practical, privacy-aware multilingual NLP pipeline with real-time latency constraints and governance mechanisms.

## Key Concepts
- **Multilingual encoders & per-language classifiers**: Shared XLM-RoBERTa backbone with lightweight task-specific heads per language
- **Latency budgeting**: Per-language SLA tracking (e.g., EN <100ms, DE <150ms)
- **Privacy by design**: Differential privacy-friendly logging, no raw data persistence
- **Drift detection & rollout**: Statistical monitoring with safe deployment/rollback strategies
- **Explainability**: Feature importance via gradient-based attribution

